2 CONT
2 CONT The father of Sampsiceramus I, Aziz also known as Azizus the Arab[15] and Azizus the Phylarch of the Arabs[15] was an ally to the last Seleucid Greek Monarchs of Syria. Aziz is associated with the rule of the Seleucid Kings Philip
2 CONC  I Philadelphus and his brother Demetrius III Eucaerus.[15] Aziz may have assisted Philip I some years before about 87 BC, in the defeat of Demetrius III who ended his days in Parthian exile.[15] Aziz assisted in putting the last 
2 CONC Seleucid King, Philip II Philoromaeus, the son of Philip I on the throne, by arranging to meet him and putting the Diadem on his head.[15] However Philip II saw that Aziz befriended him in order to murder him to gain a portion of 
2 CONC a divided Syrian Kingdom, and fled to Antioch.[15]
