2 CONC Emesa/6000000003645989988 Sampsiceramus II of Emesa].''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Do not confuse her with her daughter, also named [http://www.geni.com/people/Iotapa-of-Emesa/6000000006101246176 Iotape]. The [http://www.loebtree.com/emesa.html Loeb Family Tree] and other sources erroneously say the wife of Sa
2 CONC mpsigeratnus II was a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Aristobulus-Minor/6000000006101240937 Aristobulus Minor]. In fact, the wife of Aristobulus Minor was a daughter of Sampsigeratnus and this Iotape.''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iotapa#Wife_of_King_Sampsiceramus_II_of_Emesa Iotapa] was a princess from the Kingdom of Commagene, who lived between the 1st century BC and 1st century AD. She was one of the daughters of King Mithri
2 CONC dates III of Commagene and Queen Iotapa of Commagene. Iotapa was of Armenian, Greek and Medes descent. She was most probably born, raised and educated in Samosata, the capital of the Kingdom of Commagene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa married the King Sampsiceramus II from the Royal family of Emesa, Syria who ruled from 14-42. Through her marriage to Sampsiceramus II, she became Queen of Emesa. Iotapa with Sampsiceramus II had four children; two daughter
2 CONC s: Iotapa, Mamaea and two sons: Gaius Julius Azizus, Gaius Julius Sohaemus.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Additional Sources ==
2 CONT
