2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Iotapa=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa (born around 20 BC-unknown date of death) was a princess of Commagene, daughter of King Mithridates III of Commagene, Queen consort of Syrian King Sampsiceramus II of Emesa.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa was a princess from the Kingdom of Commagene, who lived in the second half of the 1st century BC and the first half of the 1st century. She was one of the daughters of King Mithridates III of Commagene and Queen Iotapa of C
2 CONC ommagene. Iotapa was of Armenian, Greek and Median descent. She was most probably born, raised and educated in Samosata, the capital of the Kingdom of Commagene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa married the King Sampsiceramus II from the Royal family of Emesa, Syria, who ruled from 14-42. Through her marriage to Sampsiceramus II, she became Queen of Emesa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa with Sampsiceramus II had four children; two daughters: Iotapa, Mamaea and two sons: Gaius Julius Azizus, Gaius Julius Sohaemus.
2 CONT
2 CONT From a surviving inscription dated from the reign of her husband, Sampsiceramus II along with Iotapa are known as a happy couple.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iotapa_(spouse_of_Sampsiceramus_II)
