2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Iotapa=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa (who lived in the 1st century) was a daughter of King Sampsiceramus II of Emesa who married the Herodian Prince Aristobulus Minor.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa was a Syrian Princess from the Royal family of Emesa who lived in the 1st century. She was the daughter of King Sampsiceramus II and Queen Iotapa who ruled Emesa. She was of Syrian, Armenian, Greek and Median descent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa was born and raised in Emesa (modern Homs Syria).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa married the Herodian Prince Aristobulus Minor, who was of Jewish, Nabataean and Edomite ancestry. He was a grandson of King of Judea, Herod the Great. This marriage for Aristobulus Minor was a promising marriage in dynastic
2 CONC  terms. Iotapa and Aristobulus chose to live as private citizens in the Middle East.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iotapa and Aristobulus had a daughter called Iotapa, was born deaf and mute. Apart from their daughter, they had no further descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iotapa_(daughter_of_Sampsiceramus_II)
