1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aristobulus_Minor  ''' Aristobulus Minor or Aristobulus the Younger''']  (flourished 1st century BC and 1st century AD, died after 44) was a prince from the Herodian Dynasty. He was of
2 CONC  Jewish, Nabataean and Edomite ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the youngest son born to prince Aristobulus IV and princess Berenice of Judea. His parents were first cousins and thus Aristobulus was a grandson to Herod the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT When growing up, he was educated along with his eldest brothers, Agrippa I and Herod of Chalcis in Rome, along with future Roman Emperor Claudius. (He and his siblings were the ward / hostages of Antonia Minor).
2 CONT
2 CONT Claudius and Aristobulus became friends and he became in high favor with the future emperor. Claudius and Aristobulus had sent letters to each other.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aristobulus lived at enmity with Agrippa I. Aristobulus denounced Agrippa I and forced him to leave from the protection of Flaccus, the Proconsul of Syria. Agrippa I was charged with bribing the Damascenes to support their cause w
2 CONC ith the Proconsul against the Sidonians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aristobulus married Iotapa, a Syrian Princess from the Royal family of Emesa and daughter of King Sampsiceramus II and Queen Iotapa who ruled Emesa from 14-42. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This marriage for Aristobulus was a promising marriage in dynastic terms. Iotapa and Aristobulus chose to live as private citizens in the Middle East. Iotapa and Aristobulus had a daughter called Iotapa, who was deaf and mute. Apa
2 CONC rt from their daughter, they had no further descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the reign of Emperor Caligula 37-41, Aristobulus had opposed the emperor in setting up statues of himself in the Temple in Jerusalem. He survived his brother Agrippa I, who died in 44.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Additional Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * D. C. O'Driscoll, [http://dcodriscoll.pbworks.com/w/page/9955710/Emesa Emesa]
