1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Julius Agrippa=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Julius Agrippa was a Syrian nobleman from the Royal family of Emesa who lived in the 2nd century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippa was an Emesene nobleman who was a direct descendant of the Emesene Roman Priest-Client King Sohaemus of Emesa, also known as Gaius Julius Sohaemus. He was the brother of a Julius and the paternal uncle of Julius Bassianus,
2 CONC  the Emesene High Priest of El-Gebal. El-Gebal is the Aramaic name for the Syrian Sun God.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippa served as a Primipilaris, a former leading Centurion. Agrippa was a man of some wealth as his owned an estate.[6] When Agrippa died perhaps sometime before the late 180s, his name appears to be registered at the time of th
2 CONC e Roman Jurist Quintus Cervidius Scaevola.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippa’s estate was left to the Roman Empress Julia Domna,[8] as he was the paternal great-uncle to Domna and her elder sister Julia Maesa. Agrippa is not to be confused with the powerful Lucius Julius Gainius Fabius Agrippa of A
2 CONC pamea.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Agrippa
