1 NAME Julia Cornelia Paula
2 GIVN Julia Cornelia Paula
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Julia Cornelia Paula=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Cornelia Paula or Julia Paula was a distinguished Roman noblewoman who became Empress of Rome as the first wife of the Roman emperor Elagabalus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Cornelia Paula was Empress of Rome from 219-220.Cornelia Paula was a member of the gens Cornelia through her maternal line. Her father, Julius Paulus, was a Roman Nobleman of Greek descent and a historically noted jurist act
2 CONC ive throughout the Severan Dynasty becoming a praetorian prefect in Rome. She was thus of both Patrician Roman and Greek descent and as such was a scion of the established upper Roman aristocracy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In early 219, Julia Maesa, eldest sister of Roman Empress Julia Domna, arranged for Cornelia Paula to marry her grandson, the new emperor Elagabalus. Their wedding was lavishly celebrated in Rome. Cornelia Paula became Elagabalus'
2 CONC  first wife and was given the honorific title of Augusta and the family name "Julia".
2 CONT
2 CONT In late 220, Elagabalus divorced Julia Cornelia Paula to marry the Vestal Virgin Aquilia Severa in a union that was considered scandalous because she was still a Vestal. Apart from falling in love with Severa, Elagabalus married S
2 CONC evera as a part of the religious process of worshiping the Syrian Sun God El-Gabal and integrating El-Gabal into Roman religion.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the divorce, Elagabalus removed Paula's Augusta title. As they had no children, she withdrew from public life and her fate afterwards is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Cornelia_Paula
