1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Rusticus_(Archbishop_of_Lyon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Rusticus (ca 455 – 25 April 501) was the Archbishop of Lyon, since the year of 494, the successor of Saint Lupicinus of Lyon (491 – 494). Later canonized, his Feast Day is 25 April. He was the son of Aquilinus (ca 430 – ca 4
2 CONC 70), Nobleman at Lyon schoolfellow and friend of Sidonius Apollinaris(ca 400), who was a Vicarius of a Province in Gaul under the father of Sidonius Apollinaris between 423 and 448, and wife Tullia (b. 410), and the great-grandson
2 CONC  of Decimus Rusticus and wife Artemia, and also of Saint Eucherius and wife Gallia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the brother of St. Viventiolus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married before 480 to a daughter (born ca 460) of Ruricius, Bishop of Limoges (then Augustoritum) and wife Ommance, they were the parents of three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Sacerdos, Archbishop of Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT Leontius, Archbishop of Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT Artemia, the wife of Florentinus, born in 485, a Senator, who were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gondulf of Provence, Duke, Bishop of Metz
2 CONT
2 CONT ..., wife of Munderic, Pretender of Austrasia
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Nicetius, Archbishop of Lyon
