2 CONT
2 CONT Archbishop of Lyons, France. He was a friend of St. Avitus of Vienne, and they convoked the Council of Epaone in 517 together. Saint Viventiolus (French: Saint Vivientol) (460 – July 12, 524) was the Archbishop of Lyon (ancient Lu
2 CONC gdunum), from the year of 514. Later canonized, his Feast Day is July 12. He was the son of Aquilinus (ca 430 – ca 470), Nobleman at Lyon, schoolfellow and friend of Sidonius Apollinaris, the grandson of ... of Lyon (Lugdunum) (b.
2 CONC  ca 400), who was a Vicarius of a Province in Gaul under the father of Sidonius Apollinaris between 423 and 448, and wife Tullia of Lyon (Lugdunum) (b. say 410), and the paternal grandson of Decimus Rusticus and wife Artemia, and 
2 CONC also great-grandson of Eucherius of Lyon and wife Gallia? on his maternal line.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the brother of St. Rusticus, Archbishop of Lyon. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viventiolus
