1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Bodegisel I''', formerly thought to have been the father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Baudegisel-II-Duke-of-Aquitaine/4636046500120041965 Bodegisel II], was brother to [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Gondolf
2 CONC us-Bishop-of-Tongres/6000000003182262359 Gondolfus], the other possible father of Bodegisel II. Here is the explanation: The father of our presumed ancestor Bodegisel II was either Bodegisel I of Aquitaine or Saint Gondolfus (Gand
2 CONC alf), apparently brothers of each other. His mother was apparently Palatina of Troyes (married to either of the possible fathers or to both of them). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteral/Lupis/Stirpe_Luporum.html#CAPOSTIPITE_DEI_LUPI_DI_SORAGNA_1198
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.2. Una femmina la cui parentela e matrimonio sono confermate da Gregorio di Tour, “Godegisilum, Lupi Ducis generum” cfr. Gregory of Tours IX, 12, RHGF II, p. 339.
2 CONT '''' = Godegisel (in seconde nozze) ''''
2 CONT Il suo nome suggerisce una connessione con i Re di Burgundia, uno de quali si chiamava [https://www.geni.com/people/Godegisel-king-of-the-Burgundians/6000000000277772708  Godegisel]. In prime nozze aveva sposato Palatina, figlia d
2 CONC i Gallimagnus, alla quale Fortunato dedicò un componimento storico: “Palatina filia Gallimagni, uxore Godegisili Ducis 
2 CONT
2 CONT ("suggests a connection" is not necessarily the same)
